WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:15.950
We are the last best hope of the world and
we're in the very, very unfortunate period

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:18.050
of turning our back on first principles.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.900
The government is at the point of becoming
an unlimited government.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:28.040
It is a crisis unlike any one that is previously
met.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:34.410
Any political renewal in the United States
will start from the Declaration and the Constitution.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.180
We have our natural inherent rights from God.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:40.590
The explicit purpose of government is to preserve
those rights.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:47.620
Governments are instituted among men to secure
their rights, not give us rights.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:52.450
Hillsdale was founded in 1844 on the western
frontier with a charter that says, "We'll

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:59.489
take our student body without regard to race,
sex or national origin."

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:10.030
When the Civil War broke out, every male student
left Hillsdale to enlist.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.689
The Carter Administration said, "We get to
regulate you comprehensively."

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:22.159
The heavy hand of liberalism would have been
brought to bear on education at Hillsdale.

00:01:22.159 --> 00:01:28.060
And we got rid of the money, so now there's
no indirect money from the government coming

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.060
into the college.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:34.819
And to Hillsdale's credit, it did not concede
an inch on that.

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:42.850
What do we want the college to be like in
ten years?

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:49.340
What is now an exciting on-campus phenomenon
will be recognized nationwide.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.149
It was academic in the best sense.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:57.209
It sort of attempted to take one back to first
principles and to state them cogently, so

00:01:57.209 --> 00:01:59.009
that one could follow the argument.

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:02.329
Could you tell me a bit about your graduate
school statesmanship?

00:02:02.329 --> 00:02:07.909
It gives a degree in the grade books that
are necessary to understand the American Revolution

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:09.000
and politics.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.709
They keep saying all we need is more regulation.

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:11.980
It seems like the government's-

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.530
It's in the belly of the beast.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.360
Speaking truth to power.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.890
Hello and welcome to Constitution 201, Hillsdale's
online course on the Constitution.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:26.580
Their first Constitution course ... 200,000
people signed up to listen to the great scholars

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.580
of Hillsdale.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.030
Each one of these bubbles is full of the gas
methane.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:34.990
And it sounds odd to say that this little
college in this little corner of southeastern

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:39.040
Michigan can lead a renewal, but it can.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.930
Hillsdale is producing a generation of missionaries
for liberty.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:48.500
A small, [inaudible 00:02:43] minority that
will radiate through the whole Republic.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:52.610
That is what our purpose is here, to become
men and women of character who make a difference

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.970
in this country.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:59.420
We are going to have to have a revival of
the principles of human freedom, and because

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:06.180
our college has never forgotten those principles,
never abandoned that task, we're going to

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.120
help provide that spark.

